# GEC Component Rules

## shadcn/ui

- Check registry and install via CLI before building custom UI:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add [component]
```

- Custom components only when shadcn has no fit
- `src/components/ui/` may already be customized (e.g. button `glass`) — **don’t reset to pristine**; wrap/extend for small tweaks
- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils`

## Server vs client

- Default to Server Components for thin pages that only compose sections
- `"use client"` only for state, events, browser APIs, theme, carousels, forms, Framer Motion interactivity
- Product/project list pages that use hooks stay client — match existing `useProducts` / `useProjects` pattern

## File & export conventions

- New code: **one concern per file**; kebab-case filenames (`why-us.jsx`, `hero-section.jsx`)
- Prefer **named exports** (`export function HeroSection`)
- Path alias `@/` → `src/`
- Do **not** split large legacy files (`system.jsx`, `card-product.jsx`) unless asked

## Feature folders

```
components/home/              # home section clients
components/ganvex-mat/    # product landing sections
components/news/              # News & Blog listing + detail
components/ui/                # shadcn
```

Route page stays thin; compose sections:

```jsx
// app/ganvex-mat/page.js — metadata + <GanvexMatPage />
// components/ganvex-mat/ganvex-mat-page.jsx — stacks sections
// app/news/page.js — metadata + <NewsPage />
```

## Data in components

- Sheets-backed lists: hooks → `/api/…`
- Ganvex Mat: import from `@/lib/ganvexMatData` (JSON under `ganvex_mat/`)
- News & Blog: `@/lib/cmsArticles` + `/api/articles*` (CMS `brandId`) → `useArticles`
- Banners: `@/lib/cmsBanners` + `/api/banners*` → `useBanner` (placement keys: homepage, popup, mega-menu, bottom)
